id: pm-web-h4vh
title: Investigate mixed-writer delivery SLO on an isolated capacity host
description: "The capacity harness measured 100 distinct authenticated subscribers, 10 mixed writer lanes and 50 committed updates after the late-fact replay repair. All 5000 deliveries arrived with zero loss or duplicates, but to-all p99 was 2163.5 ms against a 2000 ms SLO. The ladder correctly stopped before 1000 subscribers. High host scheduling or I/O pressure was observed without a proven saturated server resource. Reproduce from docs/capacity/2026-10-15-local.md on an isolated host; compare service, writer and storage timing before changing production limits. Related feature pm-web-lh4b and companion pm-cli-website-ghe1. Larger rungs and hosted capacity remain unmeasured."
type: Issue
status: open
priority: 2
tags[3]: capacity,performance,realtime
created_at: "2026-10-15T09:09:03.386Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-16T08:12:25.172Z"
author: codex-agent
comments[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-16T08:11:29.603Z",codex-agent,"Additional real-PostgreSQL acceptance evidence from the route/bootstrap coverage candidate: the second final-floor npm run passes all 634 coverage tests and all four dimensions, then fails only test/capacity.acceptance.ts line 16: every delivery must meet the unchanged 2000 ms SLO. Earlier assertions pass for five committed writes, zero failed writes/lost/disconnected subscribers/duplicates, and five delivery samples. This is latency failure evidence, not mutation-loss evidence. The first final-floor npm and Bun gates pass, and both Node 22/26 CI matrix jobs pass their npm and Bun release gates on source/test commit e053bb1. Reproduction: npm run release:check with isolated Git identity and explicit fleet discovery; the second Bun repetition is still running. No SLO, capacity assertion or production behavior was changed."
